WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.912
(wolves howling)

00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:06.701
- There's something about
being part of nature,

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.992
there's something about
being around these animals.

00:00:08.992 --> 00:00:10.491
To even the most wounded veteran,

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.141
they feel different,

00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:16.068
keeps them part of something
greater than themselves.

00:00:16.068 --> 00:00:18.818
(wolves howling)

00:00:21.766 --> 00:00:25.155
The idea is that you've
gotta give someone who's been

00:00:25.155 --> 00:00:29.683
through a severe trauma,
an opportunity to heal,

00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:32.075
and we believe that
Warriors and Wolves program

00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:34.991
in a back to nature setting, it does that.

00:00:34.991 --> 00:00:37.694
We have 40 animals at this facility.

00:00:37.694 --> 00:00:39.105
- There you go, you got it.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:39.995
You'll get that.

00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:42.665
- [Matthew] We've rescued
wolves off of chains in Alaska

00:00:42.665 --> 00:00:44.425
as part of a roadside attraction.

00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:48.774
We rescued wolf dogs from a
backyard breeder in San Diego.

00:00:48.774 --> 00:00:50.644
I think for all the veterans
that we bring out here,

00:00:50.644 --> 00:00:53.443
whether they work here or
they're here for a support group,

00:00:53.443 --> 00:00:57.443
what rings true is if
they can heal, I can heal.

00:00:59.071 --> 00:01:00.902
- The wolves, they notice you're injured,

00:01:00.902 --> 00:01:02.222
or something's wrong with you,

00:01:02.222 --> 00:01:03.642
and they have that trauma.

00:01:03.642 --> 00:01:06.043
So, you know, we had some type of trauma in life,

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:07.982
we kinda get that connection

00:01:07.982 --> 00:01:11.809
and one wolf will be your friend for life.

00:01:11.809 --> 00:01:13.759
- [Matthew] What happens is one animal

00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:15.483
picks that one veteran,

00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:18.033
never again does that
animal pick someone else,

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.611
never again does that animal want to show

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:21.971
the same kind of
affection to someone else.

00:01:21.971 --> 00:01:23.937
- What a good boy!

00:01:23.937 --> 00:01:27.708
Conventional therapy isn't
really something for me.

00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:29.319
It didn't help to be honest.

00:01:29.319 --> 00:01:31.986
After 10 years of military life,

00:01:33.087 --> 00:01:35.319
it was sort of a tough transition.

00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:39.152
Had I continued down my
course of being angry,

00:01:40.098 --> 00:01:41.554
drinking myself to death,

00:01:41.554 --> 00:01:45.054
may have been the last chapter of my life.

00:01:49.789 --> 00:01:52.359
- There are things I've
seen that I can't unsee.

00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:55.287
There are things I've
done that I cannot undo.

00:01:55.287 --> 00:01:58.278
Just saying that, well I did
it in the name of my country,

00:01:58.278 --> 00:02:00.096
doesn't help you sleep at night.

00:02:00.096 --> 00:02:03.125
But what does help you
sleep is having a companion.

00:02:03.125 --> 00:02:07.292
- They kinda teach you how
to be calm and confident.

00:02:09.731 --> 00:02:13.399
It's got some deeper meaning
when they accept you.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:17.566
They accept you into the
family, as part of the pack.

